{"id":"d01","name":"First Repeated Event","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["event_ids"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A stream delivers <code>event_ids</code> in order. Some events are delivered twice. Your task is to return the first id that is seen a second time while reading the list from left to right, or <code>\"\"</code> if no id repeats.</p>\n<p>The list can have up to <code>10<sup>5</sup></code> ids: aim for <code>O(n)</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>event_ids = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"b\", \"a\"]</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">\"b\"</pre><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.string event_ids<br><b>[output]</b> string</div>","starter":"def solution(event_ids):\n    # write your code here\n    return \"\"\n","hints":["Un set des identifiants déjà vus : l'appartenance coûte O(1).","Le premier à revenir, c'est celui dont la DEUXIÈME apparition arrive en premier, pas celui qui apparaît en premier."],"summary_fr":"Renvoyer le premier identifiant qui apparaît une deuxième fois en lisant la liste de gauche à droite, ou une chaîne vide.","tags":["DSA","ensemble (set)","O(n)"],"minutes":10,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"event_ids":["a","b","c","b","a"]},"expected":{"value":"b"}},{"input":{"event_ids":["x","y"]},"expected":{"value":""}}],"hidden_n":9,"hidden":"","solution":"ImRlZiBzb2x1dGlvbihldmVudF9pZHMpOlxuICAgIHNlZW4gPSBzZXQoKVxuICAgIGZvciBlIGluIGV2ZW50X2lkczpcbiAgICAgICAgaWYgZSBpbiBzZWVuOlxuICAgICAgICAgICAgcmV0dXJuIGVcbiAgICAgICAgc2Vlbi5hZGQoZSlcbiAgICByZXR1cm4gXCJcIlxuIg=="}